Z||000000||Zorba||09-13-2000||12:27 AM||||So...I got the infamous stripped headlight motor gear - the motor stays running after you turn the switch off - After cracking the case open and examining the plastic gear inside, I could see where it is stripped. So far so good. Whatever S*@$E(#)$ GM puts in the there for grease now looks like thick salt. Well, I managed to remove the plastic gear with its shaft but now  I got a problem:<BR>How do you remove the plastic gear from the metal shaft???? I am buying rodney dickmans replacement gears but I am puzzled as to how I get the old one removed... ||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||09-13-2000||08:42 AM||||Try this site:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/headlights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/biz/fierosails/headlights.html</A> <P>Good luck,<P>Carroll||||reg||1
